hadiths[27]{hadithnumber,text}:
"166","The Islam will begin to appear as a stranger, then it will return as a stranger, just as it began. Good luck to the strangers. They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, who are the strangers?"" He said, ""Those who reform when people go astray, and those for whom I am responsible will make the faith reach the furthest point, just as the river flows to its mouth. And those for whom I am responsible will make the Islam reach what is between the two mosques, just as the living flows to its depths."""""
"167","Relating to me 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Uthman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): ""Indeed, the religion will become strange and will be strange, just as the morning dew is strange."""""
"168","From Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), (in his own words): ""Islam was preserved in its original form and increased. He was asked, 'What are the ghuraba'?' He replied, 'The ghuraba are from the qaba'il.'"""""
"169","Alqamah al-Muzani reported: A man told me: I was present at the gathering of Umar ibn al-Khatab in Medina, and he said to a man from the people: ""O so-and-so! How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) describe the early stages of Islam? The man replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Islam began as a fear, then as a precaution, then as a matter of course, then as a standard, then as a reckoning."" Umar said: ""What comes after reckoning is only destruction."" (Musnad Ahmad: 15,895)"
"170","Kurz ibn Alqama al-Khuzai said: 'Araabi said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there no end to Islam?"" He said: ""Yes, as for every household, whether Arab or non-Arab, if Allah wills good for them, He will guide them to Islam."" He said: ""Then what?"" O Messenger of Allah! He said: ""Then tribulations will occur, like the darkness of night."" 'Araabi said: ""Indeed, indeed, and by Allah, if Allah wills."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will certainly return to it, and some of you will be struck with the whip, and some of you will strike others."""""
"171","And from him, another route, in which he said, ""Some of you will be killed by the necks of others."" Sufyan said, ""I asked al-Zuhri, 'What is the meaning of 'to be killed by the necks of others'? He replied, 'The living will be killed by the necks of the dead, as long as you rise.'"" (Musnad Ahmed: 16012)"
"172","And from him, from a third way, in the same manner. And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The most superior of people on that day will be a mu'min, a mu'tazil, in a group from one of the groups, who is pious to his Lord, blessed and exalted, and who leaves the people in his shade."""""
"173","Our companion Suleiman b. Habib narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, ""The ornaments of Islam will be taken away one by one. Whenever one ornament is removed, people will cling to the one that remains, and the first to be removed will be the judgment, and the last will be the prayer."""""
"174","The Islam will be torn apart, strand by strand, just as a rope is torn apart, strand by strand."
"175","I have heard a hadith from a long time ago. It is said that if you were among a people, whether few, many, or in between, and you were to call out to them in their faces, but you did not see anyone who would be spared in the presence of Allah, then know that the matter has been settled."
"176","Hazifah bin al-Yaman said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) narrated to us two hadiths. I saw the first of them and I am waiting for the second. He narrated to us that the promise was sent down in the root of the hearts of men, then the Quran was sent down, and they knew it from the Quran and they knew it from the Sunnah. Then he narrated to us from the raising of the promise, saying: ""A man's sleep is like a debt, and the promise is taken away from his heart, leaving only its residue, like the residue of a camel's load. Then the promise is taken away from his heart, leaving only its residue, like the residue of a camel's load. You will see people standing and they will not be able to fulfill their promise, just as you would not be able to fulfill your debt. Then he took a handful of dates and placed them on his thigh, saying: 'Then people will stand and they will not be able to fulfill their promise, just as you would not be able to fulfill your debt. Then he said: 'I have seen a time when I would not be able to fulfill my promise to any of you, except to so-and-so and so-and-so.'"
"177","The Islam will be preserved by five, or in another narration, by the head of five, or by seven, or by nine, and then if they are destroyed, the destruction will befall those who have already perished. And if they are left to their debt, they will be left to their debt for seven years. I said: ""What about what has passed and what remains?"" He said: ""What remains."""""
"178","And from him (i.e. the Prophet) a great deal of information. 'Umar said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What has passed and what remains?"" (Musnad Ahmad). (The second chain of transmission is similar). 'Umar said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Is what has passed equal to what remains?"" He said, ""Rather, it is what remains."" (Musnad Ahmad: 3707)."
"179","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the relief of Islam will come with five, then with three, then with six, then with seven, then with three. If they are destroyed, they will be destroyed in the manner of those who were destroyed. And if they are given a respite, they will be given a respite for seven years."" Omar said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what has passed away with what remains?"" He said, ""No, with what remains."""""
"180","It was narrated that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-'As (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Exalted, determined the destinies fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth."""
"181","I heard a great deal from him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Indeed, Allah, the Exalted, created His creation in a state of ignorance, then He illuminated them with a light on that day. Whoever is guided by that light on that day will be guided, and whoever is left in the darkness will be lost. Therefore, I say: The pen has dried up with the knowledge of Allah, the Exalted."""""
"182","I have the knowledge. From Thawus bin Yaman, he said: I saw people from the Prophet's companions saying: ""Everything is by predestination."" He said: And I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah said: ""Everything is by predestination, until inability and inability."" (Musnad Ahmad: 5893)"
"183","God created Adam from dust when He created him. He fixed his right side and brought forth a white offspring, as if they were the dust. Then He fixed his left side and brought forth a black offspring, as if they were the red camels. He said to those on his right side: ""To Paradise and no regret."" And He said to those on his left side: ""To the Fire and no regret."""""
"184","The man will be busy with the deeds of the inhabitants of Paradise for a while, then Allah will complete his deeds with the deeds of the inhabitants of Hell, and he will be from the inhabitants of Hell. The man will be busy with the deeds of the inhabitants of Hell for a while, then Allah will complete his deeds with the deeds of the inhabitants of Paradise, and he will be from the inhabitants of Paradise."
"185","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""It is not for you to be amazed by anyone until you see what is destined for him. The doer of good deeds will do good deeds for a short period of his life or for a brief duration of his day, doing a righteous deed, and if he dies, he will enter Paradise. Then he will change and do a wicked deed. The slave will do a wicked deed for a short period of his life or for a brief duration of his day, doing a wicked deed, and if he dies, he will enter Hell. Then he will change and do a righteous deed. If Allah intends good for a slave, He will make him do good deeds before his death."" They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, how will He make him do good deeds?"" He said, ""He will make him do a righteous deed, then He will take it back from him."""""
"186","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man may perform the deeds of the inhabitants of Paradise, and indeed, he may be written down among the inhabitants of the Fire. But if he dies before his death, he will turn back and perform the deeds of the inhabitants of the Fire, and then he will die and enter the Fire. And indeed, a man may perform the deeds of the inhabitants of the Fire, and indeed, he may be written down among the inhabitants of Paradise. But if he dies before his death, he will turn back and perform the deeds of the inhabitants of Paradise, and then he will die and enter it."""""
"187","A man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) fell ill, and his companions came to visit him, weeping. Someone asked him, ""What is making you weep, O servant of Allah?"" He replied, ""No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say, 'Take from the edge of your beard, then trim it until it reaches my eye.' He said, 'This is for this, and there is no benefit in it, and then take from the back of your head, that is, from the back of your head, and say, ""This is for this, and there is no benefit in it.""'"" He said, ""I do not know which of the two is better."""""
"188","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""He grasped with his hand twice. He said: 'This is in Paradise, and I have no choice, and this is in the Fire, and I have no choice.'"""""
"189","I did not see anything that resembles the prohibition of the thing that I saw, which Abu Hurairah narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""Verily, Allah has written for every son of Adam his inheritance from sin, it will reach him, there is no way to avoid it. The sin of the eye is the glance, the sin of the tongue is the word, the sin of the heart is the intention, and the sin of the private parts is the act. It will either confirm or deny it."""""
"190","Abdullah narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khuzama narrated to us, saying: My father said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! Sufyan said: I asked the Messenger of Allah: What is the treatment for a wound, what is the treatment for a plague, and what is the treatment for a fever? The Messenger of Allah replied: ""It is from the decree of Allah, blessed and exalted."""""
"191","Ibn Abbas said that one day he rode behind the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Oh young man! I am teaching you words that will benefit you. Protect Allah and He will protect you. Protect Allah and you will find Him watching over you. And when you ask, ask Allah. And when you seek help, seek help from Allah. And know that if the people were to gather together to benefit you, they would not benefit you except with something that Allah has written for you. And if they were to gather together to harm you, they would not harm you except with something that Allah has written for you. The pens have been lifted and the pages have been sealed."""""
"192","From him (Ahmad) on another occasion: ""You will be acquainted with Allah in ease, and He will be acquainted with you in hardship. If all creation were to join forces to benefit you with something, Allah would not record it for you, nor would they be able to do so. And if all creation were to join forces to harm you with something, Allah would not record it for you, nor would they be able to do so. Know that in patience there is much good, and that victory is with patience, and that relief is with hardship, and that with hardship is ease."""""
